<h1>Week 26</h1>

<p><strong>From:</strong> Lana</p>
<p><strong>Artist:</strong> The Cure</p>
<p><strong>Album:</strong> <em>Disintegration</em></p>

<p>Kayla,</p>

<p>
This week is one of my favorite albums of all time: <em>Disintegration</em> by The Cure.
</p>

<p>
The opening song “Plainsong” always stops me dead in my tracks. It is a soft, beautiful body blow to listen to this masterpiece that is about to unfold. It sets the mood and lays the foundation of just how remarkably talented The Cure is.
</p>

<p>
My top favorites:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Plainsong</li>
<li>Prayers for Rain</li>
<li>Disintegration</li>
<li>Untitled</li>
</ul>

<p>
Songs that make me think of Chloe:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Pictures of You</li>
<li>Same Deep Water as You</li>
</ul>

<p>
Can’t disregard “Lullaby” or “Fascination Street.” Robert Smith is so animated when they play them live. That is what I think of when I hear those two.
</p>

<p>
You will recognize “Lovesong” on this one, which has some of the most beautiful lyrics.
</p>

<p>
This is #116 on Rolling Stone’s Top 500. I bet it will end up in the top 20 at some point.
</p>

<p>
If you aren’t a Cure fan yet, this one might put you over the edge.
</p>

<p>
I love you!!
</p>

